tify and briefly explain any concepts that are closely related, dependent on, or analogous to the current topic. How do they connect or differ?":[59,69],"#Related Concepts:#Identify and briefly explain any concepts that are closely related, dependent on, or analogous to the current topic. How do they connect or differ?#{1}":[61,62],"#Related Concepts:#Identify and briefly explain any concepts that are closely related, dependent on, or analogous to the current topic. How do they connect or differ?#{2}":[63,64],"#Related Concepts:#Identify and briefly explain any concepts that are closely related, dependent on, or analogous to the current topic. How do they connect or differ?#{3}":[65,66],"#Related Concepts:#Identify and briefly explain any concepts that are closely related, dependent on, or analogous to the current topic. How do they connect or differ?#{4}":[67,69],"#Examples:":[70,84],"#Examples:#{1}":[72,73],"#Examples:#Provide practical code examples that illustrate the concept's application. Ensure the code is well-commented to explain each step and its relevance. The explanation has to be as comments in the code":[74,84],"#Examples:#Provide practical code examples that illustrate the concept's application. Ensure the code is well-commented to explain each step and its relevance. The explanation has to be as comments in the code#{1}":[76,84],"#Flashcards:":[85,107],"#Flashcards:#{1}":[87,88],"#Flashcards:#What is the primary purpose of C++ associative containers?;;To provide efficient storage and retrieval of elements based on keys, with operations typically in logarithmic time.":[89,90],"#Flashcards:#What is the main difference between std::map and std::set?;;std::map stores key-value pairs, while std::set stores only keys (where the value is the key itself).":[91,92],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers maintain the sorted order of their elements?;;They are typically implemented as self-balancing binary search trees (like Red-Black Trees) and use a comparison function to order the elements.":[93,94],"#Flashcards:#What is the difference between std::map and std::multimap?;;std::map requires unique keys, whereas std::multimap allows for duplicate keys.":[95,96],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers differ from unordered associative containers?;;Associative containers store elements in a sorted order, while unordered associative containers use hash tables and do not maintain a specific order.":[97,107],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers differ from unordered associative containers?;;Associative containers store elements in a sorted order, while unordered associative containers use hash tables and do not maintain a specific order.#{1}":[99,100],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers differ from unordered associative containers?;;Associative containers store elements in a sorted order, while unordered associative containers use hash tables and do not maintain a specific order.###Google Search Suggestions":[101,107],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers differ from unordered associative containers?;;Associative containers store elements in a sorted order, while unordered associative containers use hash tables and do not maintain a specific order.###Google Search Suggestions#{1}":[103,107]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Learn more","target":"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/grounding/search-suggestions","line":103},{"title":"Google logo","target":"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/24px.svg","line":105},{"title":"C++ associative containers explained","target":"https://www.google.com/search?q=C++%20associative%20containers%20explained&client=app-vertex-grounding&safesearch=active","line":107},{"title":"C++ std::multimap tutorial","target":"https://www.google.com/search?q=C++%20std::multimap%20tutorial&client=app-vertex-grounding&safesearch=active","line":107},{"title":"C++ std::multiset usage","target":"https://www.google.com/search?q=C++%20std::multiset%20usage&client=app-vertex-grounding&safesearch=active","line":107},{"title":"std::map vs std::set C++","target":"https://www.google.com/search?q=std::map%20vs%20std::set%20C++&client=app-vertex-grounding&safesearch=active","line":107}],"metadata":{"tags":["#will_learn","#cpp","#stl","#containers"],"language":["C++"],"review-date":null,"last-reviewed":"","scheda":"done","visit-count":0,"confidence-level":1,"consecutive-correct":0,"last-struggle-date":"","cssclasses":null},"task_lines":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1ggys82","at":1756395145036}},"smart_blocks:C++ Associative Containers.md#Purpose/Why:": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.05513771,-0.01081821,-0.02345431,-0.02627816,0.01699916,0.00912487,0.03136148,0.02750427,0.02525577,-0.07121928,-0.02251151,-0.00536235,0.03218345,0.01532191,0.01520889,-0.02128984,-0.04520642,0.04474098,-0.02462043,-0.01164411,0.08144692,-0.04975801,-0.06843439,-0.06024488,-0.02130614,0.05170947,-0.0594753,-0.03716876,-0.05204331,-0.25080001,-0.06051929,-0.00635947,0.124016,-0.00668857,-0.04272132,0.01529609,-0.01498491,0.05546772,-0.07898322,0.06563275,0.05439857,0.04452105,-0.05428777,0.00546441,-0.07089262,-0.02878219,-0.04777358,-0.01601427,-0.00796557,-0.03010576,-0.01922024,0.04943566,0.00366231,0.00279103,0.02292663,0.08593174,0.06761623,0.02474123,-0.02577624,-0.01827292,0.10225011,-0.00417246,-0.12086598,0.09518559,0.05079107,-0.0037722,0.00803752,-0.05191655,0.04327881,0.04301336,0.00022795,-0.01265725,0.03388016,0.08475301,0.01593266,-0.05973228,-0.00945463,-0.04882941,0.0050039,0.00445164,-0.00168304,-0.02394006,0.02529784,0.02421853,-0.00202242,-0.03928955,-0.04227626,-0.04185865,0.03735562,-0.01072115,0.02993513,-0.01407493,0.01783575,0.0586831,0.01045876,0.00008737,0.00832812,0.05298461,-0.07849129,0.14580935,-0.02160463,0.06200087,-0.00438451,-0.06785727,0.03458951,0.00912036,0.00618503,-0.05057681,-0.06820472,-0.02643947,-0.04898731,-0.04257556,0.01513349,0.01360692,-0.00063782,0.01671898,0.03387522,0.00726509,-0