difference between std::map and std::multimap?;;std::map requires unique keys, whereas std::multimap allows for duplicate keys.":[427,428],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers differ from unordered associative containers?;;Associative containers store elements in a sorted order, while unordered associative containers use hash tables and do not maintain a specific order.":[429,439],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers differ from unordered associative containers?;;Associative containers store elements in a sorted order, while unordered associative containers use hash tables and do not maintain a specific order.#{1}":[431,432],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers differ from unordered associative containers?;;Associative containers store elements in a sorted order, while unordered associative containers use hash tables and do not maintain a specific order.###Google Search Suggestions":[433,439],"#Flashcards:#How do associative containers differ from unordered associative containers?;;Associative containers store elements in a sorted order, while unordered associative containers use hash tables and do not maintain a specific order.###Google Search Suggestions#{1}":[435,439]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Learn more","target":"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/grounding/search-suggestions","line":435},{"title":"Google logo","target":"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/24px.svg","line":437},{"title":"C++ associative containers explained","target":"https://www.google.com/search?q=C++%20associative%20containers%20explained&client=app-vertex-grounding&safesearch=active","line":439},{"title":"C++ std::multimap tutorial","target":"https://www.google.com/search?q=C++%20std::multimap%20tutorial&client=app-vertex-grounding&safesearch=active","line":439},{"title":"C++ std::multiset usage","target":"https://www.google.com/search?q=C++%20std::multiset%20usage&client=app-vertex-grounding&safesearch=active","line":439},{"title":"std::map 